Gretchen, Warrick,<br />
<br />
Scope as follows, for your sign-off before Marcus's team runs it.<br />
<br />
Mailboxes: the five people named in the 2012-0331 summary record and its di=
stribution - the branch chief, the examiner in charge, the two staff examin=
ers and the assistant regional director. Where a person has left the Commis=
sion the mailbox is still in the archive; departure does not remove the jou=
rnal copy.<br />
<br />
Date range: January 1, 2012 through December 31, 2013. That is nine months =
either side of the examination, which is deliberate. An undertaking negotia=
ted at the close of an examination is frequently sent weeks after the closi=
ng letter, and a follow-up flag in the next cycle would show up in 2013.<br=
 />
<br />
Terms: the registrant name and its variants, the two principals' surnames, =
the registrant's domain, the examination number and its common transpositio=
ns, and the ordinary vocabulary of an undertaking - undertake, undertaking,=
 corrective action, remediate, will not resume.<br />
<br />
Search type: full text of message bodies and of attachment contents, not fi=
lename matching.<br />
<br />
One thing I say to everyone before I run one of these. The archive is compl=
ete for what passed through the messaging system. It is not a record of wha=
t was said on a telephone or handed across a table during fieldwork. A null=
 result from this archive is strong evidence that no document was emailed. =
It is not proof that no conversation occurred. Please make sure whoever wri=
tes the pleading understands the difference.<br />
